title: Keep a refunded asset account blocked

doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    `pallet_assets::refund` removed the asset account even when it was blocked, so the holder
    could burn their balance, drop the `Blocked` status together with the entry and receive the
    asset again afterwards. Refunding a blocked account now burns the balance and returns the
    deposit or consumer reference as before, but keeps a zero-balance entry that stays blocked
    until the admin thaws it, which removes the entry. A blocked holder can therefore still free
    a consumer reference forced on them by an asset owner, but can no longer lift the block.
    `freeze` fails with `NoAccount` on such an entry.

crates:
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: patch
